### What each verification proves

| Test | Property |
|---|---|
| `TestBasicAddRemove` | OR-Map add/remove/absent-remove semantics. |
| `TestOutOfOrderAndDuplicate` | remove-before-add and duplicated deltas converge. |
| `TestUnsafeLocalPruneResurrects` | Reproduces the exact bug: local tombstone GC + context-free merge resurrects a removed key (`B=[k]`, `A=[]`). |
| `TestStableFrontierPruneIsSafe` | Frontier GC drops the tombstone; a replayed stale add is still suppressed by the causal context. |
| `TestUnsafeLocalCompactionLosesDeltas` | Local buffer compaction strands a lagging replica; frontier compaction keeps the needed delta. |
| `TestConvergenceUnderAdversarialSchedule` | 8 seeds x 10,000 concurrent ops, 5 replicas, random partitions/heals, random reordering and duplicate deliveries. Every replica equals a delivery-order-independent op-log oracle. |
| `TestPruneMatchesNoPrune` | GC'd runs equal never-GC'd runs, both equal the oracle. |
| `TestPartitionHealPermutations` | Cluster sizes 2–6 with several partition cadences. |
| `TestIdempotentApply` | Repeated application of the same delta is a fixed point. |
| `TestGCBoundsMemory` | 10,000 add/remove cycles on one key leave ≤2 tombstones and ≤2 pending ops in the whole 2-replica system. |

### The adversarial oracle

The harness is independent of delivery order. It records the generated op log and builds the expected live set directly: live = every add dot that no remove observed. Each replica's live entries must deep-equal this set, catching both **resurrection** (extra live dot) and **lost updates** (missing live dot).

### Size bound

After the final heal + anti-entropy quiesce, every op dot is below the stable frontier, so `TestConvergenceUnderAdversarialSchedule` additionally asserts `TombstoneCount() == 0` and `PendingCount() == 0` on every replica while live entries still equal the oracle — the bounded-overhead property required under the 10k-op adversarial schedule.
